cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool, please cite both the software and the framework paper it operationalises."
title: "HEADWATERS — A Global Water–Conflict Susceptibility Watch"
abstract: >-
  A dynamic, global, web-based hotspot alert system that operationalises the
  Pathways to Instability framework of Beames et al. (2025) into a live
  watch-list, blending quantitative structural indicators with a real-time
  qualitative feed of water disturbances, with full source traceability. It
  reports susceptibility, not a forecast.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Keys
    given-names: Patrick W.
    email: pkeys.earth@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Global Water Security Center (GWSC)"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pkeys/watsec_dash"
keywords:
  - water security
  - conflict
  - susceptibility
  - hotspot
  - open data
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Pathways to instability: A synthetic framework to parse connections between water and conflict"
    year: 2025
    journal: "Environment and Security"
    doi: "10.1177/27538796251340790"
